    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Mickey Moniak**, whose 75.75 score makes him the premier play of the day. Facing Sasaki in a hitter-friendly park, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to park factors and platoon advantage, combined with a favorable 88% stolen base probability against a slow-working starter. **Isaac Paredes** (68.00) also projects as an elite option, drawing a prime matchup against Ure\u00f1a where his platoon edge and favorable #3 spot in the order significantly buoy his floor. Rounding out our high-leverage trio, **Josh Naylor** (61.02) remains a stable presence in the UTIL spot, as his strong platoon profile against May keeps him comfortably above our 60.0 threshold for \"Strong\" starts.\n\nWe have opted to bench **Austin Riley** (54.83), who served as the most difficult omission from the starting nine. While **Austin Riley** carries a solid projection, he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-ceiling platoon advantages offered by players like **Henry Bolte** and **Corbin Carroll**. **Corbin Carroll** (60.06) successfully cleared the \"Strong\" start bar despite a daunting matchup against Tolle, aided by wind-out conditions and an elite 50% stolen base probability that we simply cannot afford to leave on the bench. Conversely, **Travis Bazzana** (39.14) and **Zach McKinstry** (33.99) were comfortably cleared from the starting lineup, falling well below our 40.0 efficiency floor due to severe platoon disadvantages and unfavorable matchups against the likes of Skenes.\n\nThe primary risk today centers on the L/L matchup for **Vinnie Pasquantino** (59.32) and the general reliance on **Gabriel Moreno** (51.72) against Tolle. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a viable start due to his high raw base, the 15% penalty from the dynamic platoon data is a clear warning sign. We are monitoring the status of **James Wood**, who remains inactive on the IL; should any late-inning defensive shifts occur, we will be forced to rely on our bench depth, though at this time, we are confident that our starting core\u2014including the speed-heavy profiles of **Brice Turang** and **Henry Bolte**\u2014is optimized to attack our primary weakness in the stolen base category.",
